      "content": "interesting. so basically it was just a net win for everyone then? i feel like some people argue that union power actually hurt the economy or made things too complicated for small businesses, but it seems like the historical consensus is that the benefits to democracy and the middle class outweighed those issues. do u think there's any real validity to the criticism or is it just an excuse to keep things unequal?",
